      "properties": {
        "lc_note": {
          "source": "en",
          "texts": {
            "en": {
              "text": "## LC Anima LoRA Editor\n\n### 🛑🚫✋ Read this first\n- 🧪 **BETA, still in testing.** Presets and defaults can change between versions. Keep your original LoRA files.\n- Anima LoRAs only. Krea 2 has its own LC Krea2 LoRA Editor.\n- **Block Scan** renders 8 seeds for every row (no LoRA, full LoRA, then one block group off at a time). It only runs again when you change its settings, so tweak the Editor all you want after the first run.\n- Use a prompt with one clear character. The scan needs a face to score.\n- Anime faces are scored with **CCIP** (downloads once, about 150 MB, needs **onnxruntime**).\n\n**LC Anima LoRA Block Scan**\n- **same face**: how often two seeds give the same character. Lower = more variety.\n- **vs base**: how far the render moved from the model without the LoRA (0 = identical). A LoRA meant to change one thing should keep this low.\n- **vs LoRA**: how much of the LoRA's look you lose with that group off.\n- **blocks**: the suggested curve, wired into the Editor.\n- **groups**: 0-6, 7-13, 14-20, 21-27 and **outside** (the LLM adapter and final layer).\n\n**LC Anima LoRA Editor**\n- Sits where a LoRA loader would. Model in, model out.\n- **blocks_in** is wired to the scan. Unplug it to drag the bars yourself (0 to 2, double-click resets a bar).\n- **preset**: block groups to try by hand (early, look, look and character, finish).\n- **attention / mlp / outside_blocks**: scale those layers in every block at once.\n- **spike_soften**: **directions** flattens the one direction that dominates a layer. **spike_limit** 2 is a good start.\n\n**LC Face Variety Scorer 🧑‍🤝‍🧑**\n- Set to **anime (CCIP)**. Scores the Editor's test batch of 8, so you can check a fix without running the scan again.\n\n**LC LoRA Save**\n- ⚠️ NOTHING SAVES UNLESS IT IS TURNED ON! Set **enabled** to true.\n- Saves to **models/loras** with every edit baked in. Loads at 1.0 in any LoRA loader.\n- **rank**: 0 keeps it. Any other number makes a smaller file.\n\n---"
            }
          },
          "titles": {}
        },
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "English ✏️",
        "## LC Anima LoRA Editor\n\n### 🛑🚫✋ Read this first\n- 🧪 **BETA, still in testing.** Presets and defaults can change between versions. Keep your original LoRA files.\n- Anima LoRAs only. Krea 2 has its own LC Krea2 LoRA Editor.\n- **Block Scan** renders 8 seeds for every row (no LoRA, full LoRA, then one block group off at a time). It only runs again when you change its settings, so tweak the Editor all you want after the first run.\n- Use a prompt with one clear character. The scan needs a face to score.\n- Anime faces are scored with **CCIP** (downloads once, about 150 MB, needs **onnxruntime**).\n\n**LC Anima LoRA Block Scan**\n- **same face**: how often two seeds give the same character. Lower = more variety.\n- **vs base**: how far the render moved from the model without the LoRA (0 = identical). A LoRA meant to change one thing should keep this low.\n- **vs LoRA**: how much of the LoRA's look you lose with that group off.\n- **blocks**: the suggested curve, wired into the Editor.\n- **groups**: 0-6, 7-13, 14-20, 21-27 and **outside** (the LLM adapter and final layer).\n\n**LC Anima LoRA Editor**\n- Sits where a LoRA loader would. Model in, model out.\n- **blocks_in** is wired to the scan. Unplug it to drag the bars yourself (0 to 2, double-click resets a bar).\n- **preset**: block groups to try by hand (early, look, look and character, finish).\n- **attention / mlp / outside_blocks**: scale those layers in every block at once.\n- **spike_soften**: **directions** flattens the one direction that dominates a layer. **spike_limit** 2 is a good start.\n\n**LC Face Variety Scorer 🧑‍🤝‍🧑**\n- Set to **anime (CCIP)**. Scores the Editor's test batch of 8, so you can check a fix without running the scan again.\n\n**LC LoRA Save**\n- ⚠️ NOTHING SAVES UNLESS IT IS TURNED ON! Set **enabled** to true.\n- Saves to **models/loras** with every edit baked in. Loads at 1.0 in any LoRA loader.\n- **rank**: 0 keeps it. Any other number makes a smaller file.\n\n---"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "language": "English ✏️",
        "text": "## LC Anima LoRA Editor\n\n### 🛑🚫✋ Read this first\n- 🧪 **BETA, still in testing.** Presets and defaults can change between versions. Keep your original LoRA files.\n- Anima LoRAs only. Krea 2 has its own LC Krea2 LoRA Editor.\n- **Block Scan** renders 8 seeds for every row (no LoRA, full LoRA, then one block group off at a time). It only runs again when you change its settings, so tweak the Editor all you want after the first run.\n- Use a prompt with one clear character. The scan needs a face to score.\n- Anime faces are scored with **CCIP** (downloads once, about 150 MB, needs **onnxruntime**).\n\n**LC Anima LoRA Block Scan**\n- **same face**: how often two seeds give the same character. Lower = more variety.\n- **vs base**: how far the render moved from the model without the LoRA (0 = identical). A LoRA meant to change one thing should keep this low.\n- **vs LoRA**: how much of the LoRA's look you lose with that group off.\n- **blocks**: the suggested curve, wired into the Editor.\n- **groups**: 0-6, 7-13, 14-20, 21-27 and **outside** (the LLM adapter and final layer).\n\n**LC Anima LoRA Editor**\n- Sits where a LoRA loader would. Model in, model out.\n- **blocks_in** is wired to the scan. Unplug it to drag the bars yourself (0 to 2, double-click resets a bar).\n- **preset**: block groups to try by hand (early, look, look and character, finish).\n- **attention / mlp / outside_blocks**: scale those layers in every block at once.\n- **spike_soften**: **directions** flattens the one direction that dominates a layer. **spike_limit** 2 is a good start.\n\n**LC Face Variety Scorer 🧑‍🤝‍🧑**\n- Set to **anime (CCIP)**. Scores the Editor's test batch of 8, so you can check a fix without running the scan again.\n\n**LC LoRA Save**\n- ⚠️ NOTHING SAVES UNLESS IT IS TURNED ON! Set **enabled** to true.\n- Saves to **models/loras** with every edit baked in. Loads at 1.0 in any LoRA loader.\n- **rank**: 0 keeps it. Any other number makes a smaller file.\n\n---"
